    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d191">

                <pb facs="0359" n="265" sameAs="frus:frus1896/pg265"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Sir Julian Pauncefote
                        to Mr. Olney.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >British Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1896-04-11"><hi rendition="#italic">April 11,
                        1896</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear</hi> Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Olney</hi>:
                    Referring to your letter of the 9th instant, in which you inquire, at the
                    instance of the Treasury Department, whether Her Majesty’s Government have
                    issued an order in council relating to the seal fisheries in Bering Sea for
                    1896, I have the honor to state that I am not aware of any hew order in council
                    having been issued or being in contemplation.</p>
                <p>I presume that “The Bering Sea award orders in council 1894 and 1895” will
                    continue to regulate the fishery, as regards British sealing vessels.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Julian
                    Pauncefote.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
